## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention, RELAYED from B663)
8 cores. **Start a heavy run (`dotnet build`, `test`, `--list-tests`, `restore`, a mutant run, the full line) only while `uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent; say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile. **Then take ONE slot atomically** (`mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '.../heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '.../heavy-slot-3'`), write `B678 <time> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first and never touch one; a slot directory with no holder is reported, never taken. One heavy job at a time; re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot (and before EACH mutant); for a run longer than a few minutes also hold `.tools/b678/heavy.lock` (a directory, pid inside, released by a MOVE); at the end release ONLY your slot by a MOVE into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-25_B678_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm`. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY (worktree creation, the fetch), never a build or a test. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b678/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a figure that does not move for 3 beats means stuck. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line: wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!` or a done-marker. SDK and homes SEAT-LOCAL: `<project root>/.tools/dotnet/dotnet` with `-nodeReuse:false -p:UseSharedCompilation=false`, `DOTNET_CLI_USE_MSBUILD_SERVER=0`, `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1`; `DOTNET_CLI_HOME`, `NUGET_PACKAGES`, `NUGET_HTTP_CACHE_PATH`, `NUGET_PLUGINS_CACHE_PATH` under `.tools/b678/` set BEFORE the first restore and proven from each worktree's `obj/project.assets.json` `packageFolders`. Record `python3 --version`. Never leave a background job running; no artificial load. The Api project took 4 m 44 s on CI and 5 m 42 s on the builder's machine; budget the whole line, the mutant matrix (each mutant is a Release build plus the 40-case narrow run) and the whole-Api cap-removed run inside the hard stop, and say what you cut.

## GRADING (binding; capability decides, a comparison only finds candidates)
- **Blocker:** a path beyond the 4 in the PR; the round-2 delta anything but the one test path; any byte of `src`, `docs` or the contract differing from `6618f119`; the head moved; a removed line in the round-2 diff; a real value from any book, a person's name, a secret in an added line, your STATUS or evidence; a skipped, failed or `Skip =` test; a warning, failed or skipped test in the whole line on the combined tree; a build or merge failure of the combined tree (a member collision with main's new files is a Blocker); a NEW open alert on the PR ref with security severity high or higher or rule severity `error`.
- **Major:** one of the four named walks lists more than 20 (or fewer than the first 20) at 100,000 lines on the combined tree, or a route bypasses the cap; **a reachable non-equivalent mutant of the walk-cap code surviving every committed row and the `QuoteApiTests` family (G-2; SAME CLASS = the walk-cap class: a second same-class NO GO is the cap)**; a case red for another reason than it names, or whose expectation is read from the code under test; a name lost or more than 30 added; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (30 cases, +217 -0, 2,877, kill counts, "9 of 9"); a failing check-run on the head or the merge result; an analysis missing (4 of 4 required); a ticket key, finding id, mutant id, brief number or percent figure in the code lines, test names or commit message; non-ASCII in added lines; a build warning.
- **Minor:** an uncapped sibling walk not named by the ticket (ticket-shaped, unchanged since round 1); a green-at-base guard row with no killing mutant; a surviving equivalent proven so; a mutant of an out-of-scope sibling walk surviving; a case depending on machine, culture, order or clock that cannot fail on Linux. **Note:** process disclosures, the PR body's stale text and brief number, the long docs line, style, CI state stated.
- **Verdict token.** GO needs every check-run at the head completed and green, 4 of 4 analyses with both thresholds met, the merge ref built on current main (or your own combined tree green), the whole line on the combined tree green, R3 and R5 closed, 0 findings above Note. GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only. NO GO = any Blocker or Major; list every Major+ by id and say if it is the walk-cap class (**a walk-cap-class NO GO now reads "NO GO 2 of 2 on class walk-cap" and is the cap**). A required check you could not run adds ` (conditional: <reason>)` to the first AND last lines, never a bare GO; a check in progress at the verdict reads `CI pending: <names>` and is at most GO WITH FINDINGS. A mutant battery you could not finish is `conditional`, and a verdict without R3 and R5 finished is conditional at best.

## VERDICT
First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B678: pr112 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> round 2 of 2 @ f2102e3 on main <sha7> (R1 delta <2 commits, 4 paths, round-2 diff 1 path +217 -0, src/docs/contract bytes equal to 6618f119 y/n; combined tree = merge-ref tree y/n; non-ASCII 0 y/n> - R2 new words 0 y/n - R3 four walks capped at 20 at 100,000 and 200,000 on the combined tree y/n, routes covered <n of n>, mixed drafts y/n, siblings <named, unchanged> - R4 cases <40 y/n> green on the combined tree <n of 40> flaky 0 y/n names lost <n> added <30 y/n> collisions <0 y/n> - R5 mutants <k of m non-equivalent killed>, own beyond the list <n>, survivors <names|none>, equivalents <names>, cases with no killer <n>, controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak as expected y/n - R6 combined-tree build 0/0 <y/n>, Engine/Import/Api <n/n/n>, failed <n>, skipped <n>, SQL Server UNMEASURED - R7 checks <n completed success of n>, pending <names|none>, CodeQL analyses <n of 4>, new alerts high+ <n> error <n>, mergeable_state <s>, merge ref parents <current main|STALE>, conflict markers <n>, gitleaks canary rc <n> scan rc <n>, residue <none|named>) majors+: <ids or none>`. Then: Step 0 / REFUSE counts with controls / PINS (start, mid, verdict, with main each time) / predictions (written before any run) / R1-R7 each with the FAIL (clock time), evidence path, result / removed-lines table / case x mutant table / mutant table / check-run table at start and verdict / findings `B678-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, GRADING, class, fix-shape in prose, the regression that would be red, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid) / FOR TUESDAY (facts: the landing note below, ticket-shaped follow-ups, the stale PR text, how the squash meets main) / ROUND STATEMENT (**round 2 of 2, the last:** on GO or GO WITH FINDINGS say what Tuesday lands and the pinned command; on NO GO name each Major+ with its class; **if any is the walk-cap class say so in one line: "NO GO 2 of 2 on class walk-cap: the round cap; Tuesday posts a round-cap card to the product owner; no round 3 from a seat"**; if the Major is of another class say that it is a NEW class and does not spend the cap) / FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections (where the builder STATUS or this brief was wrong, with the measurement) / processes, slots, trees left / **UNMEASURED** (last section: the hosted site, Linux CI beyond the PR logs, web and python lines, SQL Server, real price books, anything you could not drive and why). **Last line of STATUS, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B678 pr112 b654/mps-draft-validation-walk-caps @ <sha7> <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 2 of 2) on main <sha7>` (finding ids with severities on the line above; the line carries none of the words that name a landing) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` + ONE question.

## LANDING HOLD (Tuesday's, not yours; write it into FOR TUESDAY in your own words and do none of it)
After GO or GO WITH FINDINGS and every check green on the head AND the combined tree, Tuesday lands by squash with the head pinned: `gh pr merge 112 -R datasecau/MPS-Commercial-Calculator --squash --match-head-commit f2102e3514bed3f27a13133ee271f4ac20f53da1` (re-pinned to whatever head you gated), the squash message free of record numbers, brief numbers, finding ids, mutant ids, card ids and percent figures, with the attribution trailer, and the PR title and body edited first (they are stale). The squash puts both commits in one on current main; if main has moved again by then the pin is re-read and the combined tree is Tuesday's to re-verify (a moved path among the 4 or among `QuoteRefusalOrder.cs` re-opens this gate). You never merge, push, comment, mark ready or re-run a check. A NO GO of the walk-cap class goes to the product owner as a round-cap card; the records seat, not you, moves tickets.

