- Datasec / MPS Commercial Calculator only; if any output shows another client's material, stop reading it and disclose its shape without quoting. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, docker, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production site or app host.** Network: the one fetch of Step 0 (and the one allowed main re-fetch), `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR` (the job-log GET needs `--allow-escape-sequences`), Jira GET (any JQL begins `project = MPSCALC AND ( ... )` with the parentheses; credentials by name in-process, never printed), NuGet restore into your own homes. `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh api -X POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` are forbidden. Never dismiss an alert. No decision-queue tool in any form, no scoreboard, no Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool.
- **Git in `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`, `config --get`); `clone --no-hardlinks` FROM it; `fetch`, `worktree add`, `checkout --detach`, `merge`, `merge-tree`, `merge-tree --write-tree` only inside your clone and `.tools/wt-b678-*`. No git verb in the project root (records repo) beyond the one allowed `status --short` read. Forbidden everywhere: `gc`, `worktree prune`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `fetch --prune`, `--shared`, `--reference`.
- Real price books are confidential: never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.tools/backup-*`; every scratch row is synthetic. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except through the Jira helper in-process. **Never delete** (quarantine to `.tools/b678/quarantine/`; do not type `rm` at all, even on a path that may not exist). **Never `cd`** (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (spaces and `!`); `dotnet` cwd via `bash -c` or Python `subprocess(cwd=...)`; write `${VAR}:path`; chains under `bash -c '...'` or a quoted heredoc; no unquoted word starting with `=` (the project root holds a file named `=`); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything that reads a file you did not write. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"), no decision-card id; clock from `date`. **RESUME** at about 80% of context or the hard stop: write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME`, restore every mutant, release the slot, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". A conditional verdict beats a RESUME with nothing shippable.
- **Standing lines (every Datasec kit):** (1) PRIOR-WORK CHECK: before you build anything, `git log --oneline` of the three product paths and the test file at the head, `git grep -n` for `WalkCap`, `MaxWalkEntriesListed` and `MaxNullEntriesListed` under `src/` and `tests/` of the combined tree, name every existing test that already pins a piece of this, read the builder's and the earlier gate's STATUS and the CLARIFICATIONS entry (positive control), the Jira ticket; **a STATUS without a PRIOR WORK section is returned unread**. (2) No message to any human: STATUS is the channel. (3) Jira writes: none (this scope grants no write). (4) Never delete; quarantine. (5) Landing is Tuesday's through CodeQL (the Datasec org ruleset; never bypass, never dismiss an alert).

